{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And if he has no daughter, then you shall give his inheritance to his brothers</b> — Our Sages received (Bava Batra 115a) that the father inherits his son when he dies without seed, and Scripture did not mention this. The reason is that in the laws of inheritance, every one who bequeaths also inherits, for the kinship is equal; since Scripture stated that the son inherits his father, the father too inherits the son. Moreover, inheritance follows the chain of seed among those who issue from his loins, not through collateral lines. If so, <b>then you shall give his inheritance to his brothers</b> denotes an inheritance that the father inherits at the grave and from him it comes to the brothers, but He did not wish to say, \"And if he has no daughter, then you shall give his inheritance to his father,\" for in the way of blessing does He speak, not in the way of extinction. Or perhaps this did not apply to those who enter the Land — that a father should inherit a son — for of them does He speak:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The phrase וּמִמֶּנּוּ תָּבֹא לָאַחִים is rendered literally; the reference is to the inheritance passing from the father (at his death) to the brothers. The final clause שֶׁבָּהֶם יְדַבֵּר is left open as Ramban leaves it syntactically incomplete."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:15.673465129Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}